 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
+## Thresholds (CI Gating)
+- `frai eval --threshold <metric>=<min>` allows gating on metric minimums; exit 1 if any fail.
+- In `frai-core`, `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` object (`{ exact_match: 0.9 }`).
+- Threshold results appear in reports (JSON: top-level `passed` and `thresholds` fields; Markdown: "Thresholds" section).
+- A metric with `null` score fails its threshold. Unknown metric ids or malformed thresholds exit 2 with a diagnostic message.
+- Designed for SDK use (custom metrics) as well as CLI (built-in metrics).
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
 2. Extend datasets loader to support configurable schema mapping.
